  "definition": "Brain-derived neurotrophic factor is a growth-supporting protein in the nerve growth factor family. It helps sustain certain brain neurons, including retinal, cholinergic, and dopaminergic cells, and also acts on motor and sensory neurons in the peripheral nervous system.",
